  "sourceInterpretation": "Official image reports ESP-IDFv6.1-dirty,exact private source revision unknown. Fixed public esp_perip_clk_init/periph_ll_clk_gate_set_default and headers fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643 establish the exact shutdown sequence. This does not identify undocumented clock or security topology.",
  "semantics": {
    "configuration": "21 exact words with fixed reset values and masks for unused-domain startup. Supports documented gate changes; unsupported resets,force controls and source changes fail. Existing UART/SHA/TIMG/MSPI/PSRAM/modem clocks retain their own canonical states. No generic register RAM.",
    "automaticGating": "TEE/LP_TEE/LP_GPIO free-running or automatic clock policy retained. Clearing this bit does not disable access permissions or invent a sleep transition.",
    "lcd": "Source selectors0/1 and integer divisor may be configured while disabled; the actual startup uses source1/div2. Activating LCDCAM,fractional/alternate sources and data operations are unsupported. No generated pixel output.",
    "usb": "UTMI-FS clock request may clear while original OTG PHY/APB/AHB reset bits remain set. This does not model OTG transfers or affect existing separate USB-Serial-JTAG.",
    "permissions": "Actual reads/writes to TEE,LP_TEE,LP_PERICLKRST,CNNT use documented PMS controls. LP GPIO physical ownership remains uncharacterized; no LP pad data plane.",
    "unsupported": [
      "ETM/trace/DMA/GPSPI/LP I2C/touch/key-manager data planes",
      "All undocumented reset/force or clock-source changes",
      "Physical clock timing,LP pad input/output,RF and sleep transitions",
      "SYSTIMER/scheduler startup and actual Plus board/display"
    ]
  },
